/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=()
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self'; img-src 'self' data:; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; frame-ancestors 'self'; form-action 'self'

# The pages themselves (/<lang>/, /<lang>/report, /<lang>/privacy, /<lang>/download and /d/) get their policy from the
# Worker instead (pagePolicy() in src/index.ts, docs/E2EE.md §15.6): scripts and workers only from fyl's own script paths, never 'self', which would
# admit scripts Cloudflare injects under /cdn-cgi/; the report form also allows Cloudflare Turnstile. The policy above
# stays for every other file, scripts and workers included (a worker's imports follow its own response's policy).

# /cli/<version>/ never changes once published; latest, version.json and install name the current version.
/cli/:version/fyl-*
  Content-Type: application/octet-stream
  Content-Disposition: attachment; filename="fyl"
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/cli/:version/SHA256SUMS
  Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/cli/install
  Content-Type: text/x-shellscript; charset=utf-8
  Content-Disposition: attachment; filename="install-fyl.sh"
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=60

# The link-preview pictures and the touch icon (scripts/og_images.mjs); their names stay, so a day of caching.
/og/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400

/apple-touch-icon.png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400

# Crawler rules (Cloudflare prepends its managed content-signals comment) and the sitemap they point to.
/robots.txt
  Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600

/sitemap.xml
  Content-Type: application/xml; charset=utf-8
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600

# The upload page (/<lang>/) and the language switch at / point agents to llms.txt in a Link header too, set by the
# Worker (LLMS_LINK in src/index.ts), which reaches agents that never parse the HTML (every page also has <link
# rel="describedby" type="text/markdown" href="/llms.txt">).

# security.txt (RFC 9116): where to report a vulnerability. Renew its Expires line before it passes, at least yearly.
/.well-known/security.txt
  Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600

# llms.txt (llmstxt.org): how agents use fyl.at, in Markdown.
/llms.txt
  Content-Type: text/markdown; charset=utf-8
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600

/cli/latest
  Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=60

/cli/version.json
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=60

/fonts/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/vendor/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# The download page's code (download.js, theme.js, i18n.js) and everything its workers load revalidate on every load (docs/E2EE.md §9.5, §15.6): a
# fixed deployment takes effect on the next page load, and no cache keeps an old script. That includes the vendored
# ChaCha20-Poly1305 the E2EE modules import. The download service worker's script sits in /_dl/, which confines it to
# that path (it never gets Service-Worker-Allowed, §9.2). The /d/ pages themselves come from the Worker (no-store),
# which also sets their Content-Security-Policy.
/download.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache

/theme.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache

/i18n.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache

/e2ee/*
  Cache-Control: no-cache

/_dl/*
  Cache-Control: no-cache

/vendor/noble-ciphers-2.4.0/*
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: no-cache
